.TH BLOCKMAPFS 1 "October 10, 2026" "Scalpel3 3.55.0" "Scalpel3 Manual"

.SH NAME
blockmapfs \- Read-only FUSE filesystem for blockmap-aware file access

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blockmapfs
mnt root

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBblockmapfs\fR is a read-only, multithreaded FUSE filesystem. It presents a
blockmap-compacted view of files below \fIroot\fR at \fImnt\fR.
.PP
Each exposed regular file has an adjacent regular blockmap named
\fIfilename.blockmap\fR. When the source is read through the mount point,
\fBblockmapfs\fR removes covered blocks from the visible byte stream. Reads
across a covered region continue at the next uncovered block.
.PP
Blockmap files, regular files without a blockmap, and symbolic links are hidden
from directory listings and pathname access. Directories remain visible so
mapped files in nested directories can be reached.
.PP
The effective coverage and a compact offset index are cached when a mapped file
is first accessed. Each open file has an independent backing descriptor, and
concurrent reads use positional I/O.

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
FUSE 3 (Linux) or a macFUSE release with FUSE 3 support (macOS) must be
installed.
.IP \(bu 2
\fImnt\fR and \fIroot\fR must be existing, non-overlapping directories.
.IP \(bu 2
Source files and blockmaps \fBMUST NOT\fR be modified, replaced, or removed
while the filesystem is mounted. Unmount before changing them, then remount.

.SH OPTIONS
\fBblockmapfs\fR takes exactly two arguments:

.TP
.I mnt
The directory where the filesystem will be mounted.

.TP
.I root
The source directory containing the raw files and their associated
\fI.blockmap\fR files.

.SH ERRORS
An invalid blockmap causes access to its source file to fail. If a cached source
or blockmap is replaced during a mount, subsequent opens fail with
\fBESTALE\fR. The filesystem never falls back to exposing unfiltered source
bytes.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero after a successful mount session and clean unmount. Returns
nonzero if validation, mounting, or filesystem operation setup fails.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR crblockmap (1),
.BR modblockmap (1),
.BR cmpblockmaps (1)

